.TH "GIT\-DELETE\-BRANCH" "1" "November 2026" "" "Git Extras"
.SH "NAME"
\fBgit\-delete\-branch\fR \- Delete branches
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBgit delete\-branch\fR <branchname>\|\.\|\.\|\.
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Deletes local and remote branch named <branchname>\. At least one <branchname> is required\. If omitted or empty, the command prints an error to stderr and exits with status 1\. Note that local deletion fails if the branch is checked out\.
.SH "OPTIONS"
<branchname>
.P
The name of the branch to delete\. At least one branch name is required\. If multiple branches are provided, then they will all be deleted\.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.nf
$ git delete\-branch integration
$ git delete\-branch integration bug/1234
.fi
